Export async, and leave durability to the kernel's COMMIT.

A sync export makes nfsd sync every create, remove and attribute change
before answering it. On the BitLocker test drive that was 29 ms a create and
10 ms a remove, against none at all with the export async: the whole cost of
copying many small files, of deleting a folder, and of Finder clearing up a
cancelled copy.

It is safe only with linux-nfsd-commit-is-durable, which syncs the whole file
and then its filesystem on every COMMIT whatever the export says, so what an
application commits is on the drive before it is told so. vendor-engine.sh
refuses an engine that carries this without that.

